+ source-site SyntaxId
    - left SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

` The reference converts a pipeline's left value where that value was produced: at the left
` operand, which for a bullet list is where its shifted first bullet lands.
match nodes[left]
    | .node-bullet-expression
        bullet-site(left, id)
    ??
        left

────────────────────
+ do written-bullets SyntaxId
    - expr SyntaxId

. bullets = expr
do match? nodes[bullets]
    | .node-argument(row)
        bullets = if row.name then 0 else row.expr
do match? nodes[bullets]
    | .node-block(row)
        bullets = if row.body.count == 1 then children[row.body.start] else 0
=? bullets if bullets != 0 && nodes[bullets] is .node-bullet-expression
= 0

────────────────────
+ do declaring-type-names [SyntaxId]

. found [SyntaxId]
for id in 1u32 .. < nodes.length
    do match? nodes[id]
        | .node-type-identifier(row)
            if row.is-declare
                found += id as SyntaxId
= found

────────────────────
+ do evaluated-surely Bool
    - value SyntaxId
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether a node of a value is evaluated whenever the value is: each node around it that tests
` something holds it in the part evaluated before the test, the left side of `&&`, `||` or
` `??`, or the object an optional read or index reads from.
for around in node + 1 .. < value + 1
    if subtree-start(around) > node || tests-nothing(around)
        continue
    . first = match nodes[around]
        | .node-binary-expression(row)
            if row.op != .if-op then row.lhs else 0
        | .node-get-expression(row)
            row.object
        | .node-index-expression(row)
            row.object
        ??
            0
    if first == 0 || node < subtree-start(first) || node > first
        = false
= true

────────────────────
+ tests-nothing Bool
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether a node of a value evaluates all it holds whenever it is evaluated: a name, a literal,
` a call, a block, which evaluates its lines in order, a read or an operator that tests
` nothing.
match nodes[node]
    | .node-integer-syntax
        true
    | .node-block
        true
    | .node-float-syntax
        true
    | .node-string-syntax
        true
    | .node-identifier
        true
    | .node-call-expression
        true
    | .node-argument
        true
    | .node-get-expression(row)
        !row.is-optional
    | .node-index-expression(row)
        !row.is-optional
    | .node-tuple-syntax
        true
    | .node-unary-expression
        true
    | .node-cast-expression
        true
    | .node-type-identifier
        true
    | .node-type-arguments
        true
    | .node-binary-expression(row)
        no-short-circuit && row.op != .if-op && row.op != .else-op

        .. no-short-circuit = row.op != .and-op && row.op != .or-op && row.op != .coalesce-op
    ??
        false

────────────────────
+ do arrival-clause Bool
    - clause SyntaxId

` Whether a loop on an event asks with its first clause, `when arrival` or `when bubbling`,
` for only the events that arrive at the object or for those that bubble too.
do match? nodes[clause]
    | .node-clause(row)
        if row.op is .when-clause
            do match? nodes[row.expr]
                | .node-identifier(name)
                    = name.name.text == "arrival" || name.name.text == "bubbling"
= false

────────────────────
+ do clause-delivery U32
    - clause SyntaxId

` Which publications a loop on an event hears where its only clause says so: 1 for
` `when arrival`, 2 for `when bubbling`, and else 0.
do match? nodes[clause]
    | .node-clause(row)
        if row.op is .when-clause && row.next == 0
            do match? nodes[row.expr]
                | .node-identifier(name)
                    if name.name.text == "arrival"
                        = 1
                    if name.name.text == "bubbling"
                        = 2
= 0

────────────────────
+ do ends-subscription Bool
    - clause SyntaxId

` Whether a loop's clauses include a `while` or an `until`, which end a subscription.
. current = clause
while current != 0
    . next SyntaxId = 0
    do match? nodes[current]
        | .node-clause(row)
            if row.op == .while-clause || row.op == .until-clause
                = true
            next = row.next
    current = next
= false

